<title>USA: AMBAC qualifies six muni issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>AMBAC qualifies six muni issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMBAC Indemnity Corp. said Thursday it qualified for bond insurance the following six municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Glendale Heights, Ill., $6 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Franklin County Unified School District No. 290, Kan., $2 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Mansfield Township, N.J., $2.74 million general improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Binghamton, N.Y., $10.423 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Seagoville, Texas, $1.4 million certificates of obligation.</p>
<p>--Temple, Texas, $5.3 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
